  <section class="wrap fiche-body">
    <div>
      <h2>The vibe</h2>
      <p>Marius à la Plage stretches out facing the sea, in the heart of the Gigaro bay, at La Croix-Valmer. Its website speaks of "feet in the sand" and the shade of the pergola, with contemporary Provençal cuisine: freshly caught fish, flavours of Provence, house signature dishes. Arthur and Sarah started the adventure in April 2012, after two years at the harbour with "Le Marius", named in tribute to Arthur's grandfather.</p>
      <p>At the end of the day, the house hosts musical aperitifs, between jazz, bossa nova and more contemporary sounds, around a chilled rosé or a seasonal cocktail. The tourist listings count 100 seats, a terrace, a sea view, independent wheelchair access and nearby parking; a shuttle stop is less than 300 m away.</p>

      <h2>What to know before you go</h2>
      <p>Provence-Alpes-Côte d'Azur Tourisme, Côte d'Azur France and Golfe de Saint-Tropez Tourisme list "animals accepted" among the restaurant's services. None specifies whether dogs are admitted only on the terrace or also indoors, or up to what size.</p>
      <p>The official website says "closed for the low season" at the moment; in season, the house is open every day from 9am to midnight, except Monday evening. The house takes no bookings by email or message: call 04 94 54 25 05.</p>
      <div class="callout">Coco's tip: when you call to book, say you are coming with your dog and ask for a table under the pergola.</div>

      <h2>Nearby</h2>
      <p>The restaurant looks onto Gigaro beach, in a bay that its website describes as unspoilt; a public transport stop is less than 500 m away according to the tourist listings.</p>
    </div>

